<article class="env-situation" id="0DCE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DCE">Situation <span data-tag="0DCE">111.45.1</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X = \mathbf{P}^ n_ k$ be $n$-dimensional projective space. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Recall that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \chi (X, \mathcal{F}) = \sum \nolimits _{i = 0}^ n (-1)^ i \dim _ k H^ i(X, \mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
  <p> Recall that the <em>Hilbert polynomial</em> of $\mathcal{F}$ is the function </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  t \longmapsto \chi (X, \mathcal{F}(t))  \]
</div>
  <p> We also recall that $\mathcal{F}(t) = \mathcal{F} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{O}_ X(t)$ where $\mathcal{O}_ X(t)$ is the $t$th twist of the structure sheaf as in Constructions, Definition <a href="/tag/01MN" data-tag="01MN">27.10.1</a>. In Varieties, Subsection <a href="/tag/08A9" data-tag="08A9">33.35.13</a> we have proved the Hilbert polynomial is a polynomial in $t$. </p>
</article>